WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.033 --> 00:00:00.300
All right.

00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:00.567
Now, we

00:00:00.567 --> 00:00:02.202
are moments away from a high stakes,

00:00:02.202 --> 00:00:04.137
one on one meeting in Moscow

00:00:04.137 --> 00:00:04.804
between Russian

00:00:04.804 --> 00:00:05.772
President Putin

00:00:05.772 --> 00:00:06.940
and Chinese President Xi

00:00:06.940 --> 00:00:07.841
as Xi arrived in Moscow

00:00:07.841 --> 00:00:10.010
for the state visit just a few hours ago.

00:00:10.010 --> 00:00:10.777
Beijing, of course,

00:00:10.777 --> 00:00:11.711
framing this trip

00:00:11.711 --> 00:00:13.880
as more of a peacemaking mission

00:00:13.880 --> 00:00:15.415
amidst the war in Ukraine.

00:00:15.415 --> 00:00:15.982
It comes

00:00:15.982 --> 00:00:17.417
just after the International

00:00:17.417 --> 00:00:18.051
Criminal Court

00:00:18.051 --> 00:00:19.519
issued an arrest warrant

00:00:19.519 --> 00:00:20.754
for Vladimir Putin,

00:00:20.754 --> 00:00:22.355
essentially charging him

00:00:22.355 --> 00:00:24.057
with the abduction of children

00:00:24.057 --> 00:00:25.725
from Ukraine.

00:00:25.792 --> 00:00:27.227
Joining us now to discuss

00:00:27.227 --> 00:00:29.963
what those charges could actually mean

00:00:29.963 --> 00:00:30.363
is Leila

00:00:30.363 --> 00:00:31.564
set out as a professor

00:00:31.564 --> 00:00:32.198
at Washington

00:00:32.198 --> 00:00:34.134
University in Saint Louis School of Law

00:00:34.134 --> 00:00:34.667
and one of the world's

00:00:34.667 --> 00:00:35.769
foremost authorities

00:00:35.769 --> 00:00:36.436
when it comes

00:00:36.436 --> 00:00:38.104
to international criminal law.

00:00:38.104 --> 00:00:38.438
It's good

00:00:38.438 --> 00:00:39.606
to have you with us this morning.

00:00:39.606 --> 00:00:42.242
So when these charges broke,

00:00:42.642 --> 00:00:44.077
there was a lot of talk

00:00:44.077 --> 00:00:46.312
about how they are largely symbolic

00:00:46.312 --> 00:00:49.049
since the reality of Putin traveling

00:00:49.049 --> 00:00:51.217
to a country.

00:00:51.217 --> 00:00:52.652
Right, an ICC country

00:00:52.652 --> 00:00:54.287
where he could potentially be arrested

00:00:54.287 --> 00:00:55.622
seems slim.

00:00:55.622 --> 00:00:56.222
Why do you think

00:00:56.222 --> 00:00:57.624
the charges were filed now?

00:00:59.426 --> 00:00:59.959
Well, the

00:00:59.959 --> 00:01:01.027
charges are filed

00:01:01.027 --> 00:01:01.928
because Ukraine

00:01:01.928 --> 00:01:03.496
referred the case to the court

00:01:03.496 --> 00:01:05.732
and actually 41 states

00:01:05.732 --> 00:01:08.168
joined the referral to the court.

00:01:08.168 --> 00:01:10.670
Ukraine asked the ICC to investigate,

00:01:11.071 --> 00:01:13.973
as did 41 members of the court

00:01:13.973 --> 00:01:15.909
states parties, if you like.

00:01:15.909 --> 00:01:18.211
And that means that the prosecutor

00:01:18.211 --> 00:01:20.313
has an obligation to investigate.

00:01:20.313 --> 00:01:21.247
And the prosecutor

00:01:21.247 --> 00:01:23.516
has to follow the facts and the law

00:01:23.516 --> 00:01:24.217
and the facts,

00:01:24.217 --> 00:01:26.086
as we've seen on our television screens.

00:01:26.086 --> 00:01:27.487
Thanks so much to CNN

00:01:27.487 --> 00:01:29.022
for your great reporting, by the way.

00:01:29.022 --> 00:01:30.056
Erica.

00:01:30.056 --> 00:01:31.391
The facts really drive

00:01:31.391 --> 00:01:34.227
this case and the facts are shocking

00:01:34.227 --> 00:01:37.964
and their illumination of war crimes.

00:01:38.298 --> 00:01:39.165
And so the prosecutor

00:01:39.165 --> 00:01:40.500
really has no obligation

00:01:40.500 --> 00:01:41.901
but to file charges.

00:01:41.901 --> 00:01:42.702
We have really seen

00:01:42.702 --> 00:01:44.003
this concerted effort.

00:01:44.003 --> 00:01:44.804
I mean, I was even meeting

00:01:44.804 --> 00:01:46.272
with Polish officials

00:01:46.272 --> 00:01:47.307
just about a year ago

00:01:47.307 --> 00:01:48.541
talking about their efforts

00:01:48.541 --> 00:01:50.443
to work to help document

00:01:50.443 --> 00:01:52.045
potential war crimes.

00:01:52.045 --> 00:01:54.681
What more do you see could be coming?

00:01:56.049 --> 00:01:58.051
I think this is the tip of the iceberg.

00:01:58.051 --> 00:01:59.886
I think it's a brilliant strategy

00:01:59.886 --> 00:02:01.688
on the part of the prosecutor to charge

00:02:01.688 --> 00:02:03.156
both Vladimir Putin

00:02:03.156 --> 00:02:04.591
and his commissioner

00:02:04.591 --> 00:02:06.893
for children's rights

00:02:06.893 --> 00:02:08.027
in this case,

00:02:08.027 --> 00:02:09.662
because there are two war crimes

00:02:09.662 --> 00:02:10.897
that have been charged.

00:02:10.897 --> 00:02:12.932
They're relatively obvious.

00:02:12.932 --> 00:02:14.534
Russia's essentially admitted

00:02:14.534 --> 00:02:15.602
to what happened.

00:02:15.602 --> 00:02:16.536
Vladimir Putin

00:02:16.536 --> 00:02:18.705
and his minister have stated

00:02:18.705 --> 00:02:20.640
that they engaged in this conduct.

00:02:20.640 --> 00:02:22.108
And so it's really obvious.

00:02:22.108 --> 00:02:22.675
And it's also a

00:02:22.675 --> 00:02:24.277
particularly heinous offense.

00:02:24.277 --> 00:02:26.479
These are actually grave breaches

00:02:26.479 --> 00:02:28.114
of the Geneva Conventions

00:02:28.114 --> 00:02:28.982
and Russia is a party

00:02:28.982 --> 00:02:30.283
to the Geneva Conventions.

00:02:30.283 --> 00:02:31.951
So Russia knows exactly

00:02:31.951 --> 00:02:33.419
that these are not okay.

00:02:33.419 --> 00:02:34.053
The transfer

00:02:34.053 --> 00:02:35.788
and deportation of children

00:02:35.788 --> 00:02:37.857
during war is unlawful.

00:02:37.857 --> 00:02:39.125
So I think these are the tip

00:02:39.125 --> 00:02:39.859
of the iceberg.

00:02:39.859 --> 00:02:41.327
I think we're going to see a lot more

00:02:41.327 --> 00:02:42.695
charges relating

00:02:42.695 --> 00:02:45.031
probably to crimes against humanity,

00:02:45.031 --> 00:02:45.798
probably to the

00:02:45.798 --> 00:02:47.534
aerial bombardment campaign

00:02:47.534 --> 00:02:49.202
and other attacks on civilians

00:02:49.202 --> 00:02:51.271
and civilian infrastructure.

00:02:51.271 --> 00:02:52.705
So while you anticipate more charges,

00:02:52.705 --> 00:02:53.740
what do you think the outcome of

00:02:53.740 --> 00:02:54.774
some of those charges will be?

00:02:54.774 --> 00:02:56.342
Because correct me if I'm wrong,

00:02:56.342 --> 00:02:58.511
but these ICC charges

00:02:58.511 --> 00:02:59.546
Putin, for example, can't be

00:02:59.546 --> 00:03:00.880
tried in absentia, correct?

00:03:02.248 --> 00:03:04.150
That's absolutely right, Erica.

00:03:04.150 --> 00:03:04.817
And, of course,

00:03:04.817 --> 00:03:06.753
we know that international justice

00:03:06.753 --> 00:03:09.022
always has to play the long game.

00:03:09.022 --> 00:03:10.056
Many times

00:03:10.056 --> 00:03:11.891
we found ourselves in this situation

00:03:11.891 --> 00:03:13.293
before with respect

00:03:13.293 --> 00:03:14.627
to Slobodan Milosevic,

00:03:14.627 --> 00:03:16.496
with respect to Charles Taylor,

00:03:16.496 --> 00:03:17.130
with respect

00:03:17.130 --> 00:03:18.331
to Ratko Mladic,

00:03:18.331 --> 00:03:19.999
we've had to wait a long time

00:03:19.999 --> 00:03:22.001
to get our defendants in the dock.

00:03:22.001 --> 00:03:24.070
That said, as a permanent court,

00:03:24.070 --> 00:03:25.405
the International Criminal Court

00:03:25.405 --> 00:03:26.339
can wait.

00:03:26.339 --> 00:03:28.274
There's no statute of limitations.

00:03:28.274 --> 00:03:30.009
And it makes it much more difficult

00:03:30.009 --> 00:03:31.711
both for President Putin

00:03:31.711 --> 00:03:33.479
and for his commissioner

00:03:33.479 --> 00:03:34.881
to travel abroad

00:03:34.881 --> 00:03:36.249
to conduct their business

00:03:36.249 --> 00:03:37.684
and subjecting them potentially

00:03:37.684 --> 00:03:39.252
to crippling sanctions

00:03:39.252 --> 00:03:40.486
at a personal level,

00:03:40.486 --> 00:03:42.789
as well as because of their state conduct

00:03:43.022 --> 00:03:44.290
everywhere they go.

00:03:44.290 --> 00:03:45.658
Really quickly before I let you go.

00:03:45.658 --> 00:03:47.694
Do you see these both these charges

00:03:47.694 --> 00:03:50.730
and the potential for additional charges

00:03:51.097 --> 00:03:53.466
in any way influencing the behavior

00:03:54.167 --> 00:03:56.736
or the orders given to Russian troops?

00:03:58.805 --> 00:04:02.442
So I don't see President Putin himself

00:04:02.442 --> 00:04:04.677
all of a sudden having a change of heart

00:04:04.944 --> 00:04:05.612
and saying, you know,

00:04:05.612 --> 00:04:06.980
this is a really bad idea.

00:04:06.980 --> 00:04:07.547
We shouldn't

00:04:07.547 --> 00:04:08.748
we shouldn't be violating

00:04:08.748 --> 00:04:10.049
international law.

00:04:10.049 --> 00:04:11.150
What I suspect, though,

00:04:11.150 --> 00:04:13.253
is that others under his command,

00:04:13.453 --> 00:04:15.121
soldiers in the field,

00:04:15.121 --> 00:04:16.489
when asked to do things

00:04:16.489 --> 00:04:16.756
that are

00:04:16.756 --> 00:04:18.691
manifestly unlawful,

00:04:18.691 --> 00:04:20.560
that are clearly breaches

00:04:20.560 --> 00:04:21.961
of international law,

00:04:21.961 --> 00:04:23.863
not just in the ICC statute,

00:04:23.863 --> 00:04:24.931
but in all the treaties

00:04:24.931 --> 00:04:25.865
that Russia is a party

00:04:25.865 --> 00:04:26.733
to Russia

00:04:26.733 --> 00:04:27.200
as a party,

00:04:27.200 --> 00:04:28.601
to the genocide convention,

00:04:28.601 --> 00:04:30.370
to the Geneva Conventions.

00:04:30.370 --> 00:04:31.704
I think a lot of the people

00:04:31.704 --> 00:04:32.905
in Russia,

00:04:32.905 --> 00:04:34.974
once they learn about these things,

00:04:34.974 --> 00:04:36.776
are going to have second thoughts

00:04:36.776 --> 00:04:37.710
about this war.

00:04:37.710 --> 00:04:39.912
And we understand from the reporting

00:04:39.912 --> 00:04:41.281
that's now ongoing

00:04:41.281 --> 00:04:43.416
that that's already happening.

00:04:43.416 --> 00:04:43.783
Ladies,

00:04:43.783 --> 00:04:45.051
that really appreciate your insight

00:04:45.051 --> 00:04:45.852
this morning. Thank you.

